tion until it reaches an edge or another band. The distinguishing assumption is that markers encode indefinitely continuing rays, so new inputs with gaps would be filled along the same slope.\", \"p1\": \"Another plausible mechanism is mirror completion: treat each colored diagonal fragment as one side of a reflected pattern across a nearby horizontal or vertical stripe, adding the missing symmetric counterpart while preserving the stripe. This assumes symmetry, not continuation; an asymmetric fragment on another input would therefore produce a different result.\", \"p2\": \"A third plausible mechanism is band-guided routing: each solid-color band acts as a region label, and isolated markers are projected diagonally only through regions associated with their color, stopping or changing behavior at band boundaries. The distinguishing assumption is that bands control propagation rather than merely serving as obstacles.\", \"p3\": \"A fourth plausible mechanism is finite-sequence extrapolation: identify the step pattern among the few marked cells and append only enough same-step cells to complete a bounded arithmetic sequence, preserving all unrelated bands. This assumes the marks describe a finite motif, so the result would differ from ray extension when the boundary leaves extra space.\"}, \"public_inputs\": [[[8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8], [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8], [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 0], [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 0, 8], [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 0, 8, 8], [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 0, 8, 8, 8], [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8], [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 